{"parentUuid":"3dac55a7-8c84-413d-8d92-40758fe79757","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab56e030d7ec24cad","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015WoJen82DMN1KYd1AkZPoH","type":"tool_result","content":"# CPMpy Releases: Late 2025 & 2026 H1\n\nBased on the provided GitHub releases page, I can only identify releases through January 2025. There are no releases documented from late 2025 or 2026 H1 in the content provided.\n\n## Available Releases (2024-2025)\n\n**v0.10.0** (January 19, 2025)\n- New Rc2 MaxSAT solver backend\n- Enhanced CNF transformation via pindakaas encoding\n- Boolean-Integer multiplication linearization\n- Hexaly solution callbacks\n- OR-Tools 9.15 compatibility fixes\n\n**v0.9.29** (January 15, 2025)\n- Hotfix addressing external breaking changes in default solver backend\n- Solver version pinning\n\n**v0.9.28** (October 17, 2024)\n- Multi-dimensional indexing fix for decision variables\n\n**v0.9.27** (October 6, 2024)\n- CPLEX ILP solver integration\n- Hexaly local search solver support\n- CLI tool for solver version information\n\nThe releases page does not contain information about MUS/QuickXplain explain tools improvements, nor does it document releases beyond January 2025."}]},"uuid":"39c89321-2928-4c04-a387-01c40c975789","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:02.971Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3dac55a7-8c84-413d-8d92-40758fe79757","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e1303053-06ec-4e1c-92e4-93d19a7fd0f7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab56e030d7ec24cad","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KnscMsE2gY33xePXfzYBz6","type":"tool_result","content":"I cannot provide the specific winners for those divisions based on the content given. While the page mentions that \"Results are available!\" with a link dated August 11, 2025, the actual results data is not included in the web page content provided.\n\nTo find the SMT-COMP 2025 winners for QF_LIA, QF_BV, and QF_LRA single query divisions, you would need to visit the \"[Results](/2025/results/)\" section linked on the homepage."}]},"uuid":"94c58264-106d-4f46-a5a5-f43604819a96","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:04.998Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e1303053-06ec-4e1c-92e4-93d19a7fd0f7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b5b3b2a5-cfc7-4662-826c-891db2493f89","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab56e030d7ec24cad","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ersszp1tK2LHwFrAe1qQKZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# CVC5 Releases: Late 2025 to Mid-2026\n\nBased on the GitHub releases page, here are the documented versions from this period:\n\n## Recent Releases\n\n**cvc5-1.3.4** (May 7, 2026)\n- Compiler requirements increased: \"GCC >= 10 and Clang >= 12\"\n- SymFPU divider encoding fixes for bitvector operations\n- Parser improvements for indexed bit-vector operators with width ≥ 2³²\n- Enabled `--solve-bv-as-int` with quantifiers and UFs\n- \"Added full proof support in CaDiCaL\" for SAT solving\n- CPC proof improvements for AUFNIRA logics\n\n**cvc5-1.3.3** (February 25, 2026)\n- Addressed `get-assertions` state-clearing bug\n- \"Lazy approach for handling `distinct` constraints\"\n- Non-linear arithmetic strategy enhancements\n- SyGuS solver corner case fixes\n\n**cvc5-1.3.2** (December 12, 2025)\n- Variable elimination bug fix for quantified formulas\n- More efficient resolution strategy (CHAIN_M_RESOLUTION) for SAT proofs\n- Linear and non-linear arithmetic solver updates\n- New multiplication lemma schema (`--nl-ext-flatten-mon`)\n\n**cvc5-1.3.1** (September 24, 2025)\n- Unicode string API migration from `std::wstring` to `std::u32string`\n- Introduced `stable-mode` build configuration\n\n**cvc5-1.3.0** (June 19, 2025)\n- Extensive CPC proof format coverage for all safe-mode theories\n- SMT-LIB 2.7 arithmetic bit-vector conversion functions\n- Multi-threaded `TermManager` support\n\nThe page does not provide specific details on QF_LIA-specific optimizations, MUS improvements, or Python binding changes for this period."}]},"uuid":"41cd047b-4cb1-441d-876b-c289096496f9","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:06.258Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b5b3b2a5-cfc7-4662-826c-891db2493f89","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f72e279b-e33c-455e-8790-a214c412eb92","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab56e030d7ec24cad","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QAvFbGyLBgm6gptgAG6KyU","type":"tool_result","content":"# Z3 Releases: Late 2025 - H1 2026 Summary\n\nBased on the GitHub releases page, here are the notable Z3 versions from this period:\n\n## Recent Releases\n\n**z3-4.16.0** (February 19, 2026) - Latest stable release\n**z3-4.15.8** (February 12, 2026)\n**z3-4.15.7** (February 9, 2026)\n**z3-4.15.6** (February 8, 2026)\n**z3-4.15.5** (February 7, 2026)\n**z3-4.15.4** (October 29, 2025)\n\n## Key Improvements Identified\n\n**Python API & Language Bindings:**\nThe release notes mention \"Add support for Algebraic Datatypes in JavaScript/TypeScript bindings\" and updates to Java API including missing method implementations for character sorts.\n\n**Performance & Solver Enhancements:**\nNotable changes include throttling mechanisms for nonlinear arithmetic lemmas, \"better bit-blasting for rotation,\" and AC (associative-commutative) completion improvements for the EUF solver.\n\n**UNSAT Core Support:**\nReferences to \"adding proofs to euf-completion\" and proof-related enhancements suggest continued development in unsatisfiability core generation.\n\n**New Tactics & Infrastructure:**\nImplementation of \"euf-completion with optional solver\" and E-matching capabilities indicate expanded tactic options.\n\n*Note: The page content shows loading errors for detailed asset information, limiting comprehensive analysis of specific QF_LIA/QF_BV benchmark improvements.*"}]},"uuid":"4c00e5e7-e4fe-4a7e-99ef-1a00b289bede","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:07.356Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f72e279b-e33c-455e-8790-a214c412eb92","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy