{"parentUuid":"0c628426-aa77-4c80-a87f-f1b45c016de8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab56e030d7ec24cad","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016ud18g5bpx6k2Qs1kLNnep","type":"tool_result","content":"# CPMpy Latest Version (2026 H1)\n\n**Current Latest Version:** 0.10.0, released January 19, 2026\n\n## Recent Versions (2025-2026)\n\n| Version | Release Date |\n|---------|--------------|\n| 0.10.0 | Jan 19, 2026 |\n| 0.9.29 | Jan 15, 2026 |\n| 0.9.28 | Oct 17, 2025 |\n| 0.9.27 | Oct 6, 2025 |\n| 0.9.26 | Aug 10, 2025 |\n| 0.9.25 | May 7, 2025 |\n| 0.9.24 | Jan 17, 2025 |\n\nThe library is described as \"a numpy-based library for modeling constraint programming problems\" and maintains active development with roughly quarterly releases throughout 2025 and early 2026."}]},"uuid":"54673dc1-1f62-4ff0-b235-2633dccedc85","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:16.803Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0c628426-aa77-4c80-a87f-f1b45c016de8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fc843f6a-00c0-4c7f-b225-90cefa1ff8b2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab56e030d7ec24cad","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L1fububhMJV1LQbwz3B23K","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPMpy 0.9.29 0.10 changelog release 2025 explain tools MUS\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Releases · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/releases\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpmpy/0.9.10/\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cpmpy\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy 0.9.28 on PyPI - Libraries.io - security & maintenance data for open source software\",\"url\":\"https://libraries.io/pypi/cpmpy\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling in Python — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Modeling and solving with CPMpy — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/modeling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · github/github-mcp-server\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · anomalyco/opencode\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/releases\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - CPMpy/cpmpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling library in Python, based on numpy, with direct solver access. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy\"},{\"title\":\"Third-Party Software Update Catalog Release History – August 2025 - Patch My PC\",\"url\":\"https://patchmypc.com/catalog-release/2025/third-party-software-update-catalog-release-history-august-2025/\"}]\n\nLet me search for more specific information about the v0.10.0 release and MUS tools.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Releases · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/releases\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpmpy/0.9.10/\"},{\"title\":\"Solving with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - CPMpy/cpmpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling library in Python, based on numpy, with direct solver access. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy\"},{\"title\":\"Modeling and solving with CPMpy — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/modeling.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling in Python — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Tools (cpmpy.tools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/tools.html\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumption variables — CPMpy 0.9.21 ...\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cpmpy\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/z3-auto-subsolver/unsat_core_extraction.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide you with information about the CPMpy releases you asked about:\n\n## CPMpy Release Summary\n\nCPMpy 0.10.0 was released on January 19, 2026, and version 0.9.29 was released on January 15, 2026.\n\n### Version 0.9.29\nVersion 0.9.29 is a hotfix release due to external breaking changes in the default solver backend.\n\n### Version 0.10.0 Key Features\nThe v0.10.0 release includes a new Rc2 MaxSAT solver, expanded to_cnf using pindakaas encoding backend, linearisation of multiplication between Boolean and Integer, solution callback for Hexaly, and documentation overview of solver capabilities.\n\n## MUS Tools Explanation\n\nCPMpy implements functionality using PySAT-like s.solve(assumptions=[...]) and s.get_core() for unsat core extraction, which opens the door to advanced use cases such as Minimal Unsatisfiable Subsets (MUS). In the tools, a simple MUS deletion based algorithm using assumptions has been implemented.\n\nThe MUS tool can be used with: `from cpmpy.tools import mus` and then `print(mus(m.constraints))`, allowing users to identify minimal unsatisfiable subsets of constraints in their constraint programming problems for debugging purposes.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b9c5da36-c337-4590-8eaf-b477101a5fc4","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:21.564Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fc843f6a-00c0-4c7f-b225-90cefa1ff8b2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
